# Test: the RFC 4552 OSPFv3 IPsec doctor diagnostic is registered and explainable.
#
# VALIDATES: spec-ospf-ext-16 AC-12 -- the doctor-ospfv3-ipsec code (warns when an
# OSPFv3 interface configures IPsec but the kernel XFRM dataplane is unavailable) is
# registered by the ospf component and explainable. The check-execution logic is covered
# by internal/plugins/ospf/doctor_ipsec_test.go (TestOSPFIPsecDoctorWarnsWhenXFRMUnavailable);
# the live XFRM install/drop path is exercised by the QEMU integration test
# internal/plugins/ospf/ipsec_integration_linux_test.go.
# PREVENTS: the IPsec doctor code regressing to unregistered/unexplainable.

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze explain doctor-ospfv3-ipsec
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:contains=doctor-ospfv3-ipsec
expect=stdout:contains=CAP_NET_ADMIN
